cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite both the accompanying technical report and this software artifact."
title: "SD-BKZ vs. BKZ: A Reproducible Lattice-Reduction Benchmark via the Li-Nguyen Rankin Profile"
abstract: >-
  The Root Hermite Factor (RHF), the dominant quality metric for
  lattice basis reduction, is structurally blind to meaningful
  differences between reduced bases. Comparing BKZ against self-dual
  BKZ (SD-BKZ) across more than 4,500 seeds on LWE-Kannan embedding
  lattices, RHF differences are below 1e-6 in all groups without
  outlier seeds, while the Li-Nguyen Rankin profile distance d(LN)
  reveals statistically significant gaps (Cohen's d up to 9.4). This
  repository ships the containerised benchmark, seed manifest,
  analysis pipeline, and accompanying technical report as a single
  reproducible artifact.
